{
  "id": "ep206",
  "duration": 51.857,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.813,
      "text": "We shortened an asteroid's orbit thirty-two minutes just by crashing into it.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's illustration of NASA's Double Asteroid Redirection Test Mission.jpg",
        "credit": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_illustration_of_NASA%27s_Double_Asteroid_Redirection_Test_Mission.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.813,
      "end": 13.358,
      "text": "In September 2022, NASA slammed a box-shaped spacecraft into Dimorphos, a moonlet seven million miles from Earth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Schematic of the DART impact geometry on Dimorphos.webp",
        "credit": "Authors of the study: Andrew F. Cheng, Harrison F. Agrusa, Brent W. Barbee, Alex J. Meyer, Tony L. Farnham, Sabina D. Raducan, Derek C. Richardson, Elisabetta Dotto, Angelo Zinzi, Vincenzo Della Corte",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schematic_of_the_DART_impact_geometry_on_Dimorphos.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 13.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.358,
      "end": 20.903,
      "text": "The DART mission targeted this 530-foot-wide rock at a staggering speed of 14,000 miles per hour.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dimorphos North-Up Image Composition reduced bloom.png",
        "credit": "NASA/Johns Hopkins APL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dimorphos_North-Up_Image_Composition_reduced_bloom.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.367,
          "end": 18.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 18.533,
          "end": 20.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.903,
      "end": 27.373,
      "text": "While telescopes like James Webb watched, an Italian CubeSat caught the moment the probe hit the surface.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Twin Tail Revealed in New Hubble Image of Didymos-Dimorphos System Following DART Impact (opo22056a).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, Jian-Yang Li (PSI), Joe Depasquale (STScI)",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Twin_Tail_Revealed_in_New_Hubble_Image_of_Didymos-Dimorphos_System_Following_DART_Impact_(opo22056a).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.9,
          "end": 27.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.373,
      "end": 34.793,
      "text": "Mission controllers only expected the violent collision to nudge the asteroid orbit by about seventy-three seconds.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Webb Captures DART Impact (weic2215c).jpeg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, CSA, and STScI",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Webb_Captures_DART_Impact_(weic2215c).jpeg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.367,
          "end": 34.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.793,
      "end": 41.288,
      "text": "But the impact blasted so much debris into space that the recoil acted like a massive rocket engine.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Evolution of the cloud of debris around Dimorphos and Didymos after the DART impact (eso2303a).tiff",
        "credit": "ESO/Opitom et al.",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evolution_of_the_cloud_of_debris_around_Dimorphos_and_Didymos_after_the_DART_impact_(eso2303a).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 38.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.267,
          "end": 41.3,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.288,
      "end": 47.388,
      "text": "This amplified the push so much that the nearly twelve-hour orbit changed by over half an hour.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "This chart offers insight into data the DART team used to determine the orbit of Dimorphos after impact.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Johns Hopkins APL/Astronomical Institute of the Academy of Sciences of the Czech Republic/Lowell Observatory/JPL/Las Cumbres Observatory/Las Campanas Observatory/European Southern Observatory Dan",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:This_chart_offers_insight_into_data_the_DART_team_used_to_determine_the_orbit_of_Dimorphos_after_impact.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.3,
          "end": 47.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.388,
      "end": 51.507,
      "text": "This is how we learned to steer a giant space rock by crashing into it.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist's illustration of NASA's Double Asteroid Redirection Test Mission.jpg",
        "credit": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%27s_illustration_of_NASA%27s_Double_Asteroid_Redirection_Test_Mission.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.4,
          "end": 51.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
